	)
	(text
		"R707 is the shared reference resistor -\nboth return leads meet here, so both\nchannels are ratiometric."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 96.52 137.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "67369f69-8533-5979-8493-8aee4357fde4")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 180.34 31.75)
		(end 238.76 154.94)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "2a3fc56e-08d0-51ce-83a2-6e546978536d")
	)
	(text
		"ADS1120 SUPPLIES AND SPI2"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 181.61 32.77 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "494a2b4f-74d8-5d30-911c-c438f86ce90f")
	)
	(text
		"OQ-04 RESOLVED: RTD, NOT NTC - Pt1000, 3-wire, class A (IEC 60751)\n  Chosen over an NTC because the ADS1120 exists to do exactly this:\n  two matched IDACs give ratiometric excitation with automatic lead\n  compensation, and a class-A RTD is accurate to +/-(0.15 + 0.002|t|)\n  degC interchangeably - no per-part beta calibration, which an NTC\n  would need to reach REQ-EL-07 1 degC. Pt1000 rather than Pt100\n  because every ohm of error in the signal path costs 10x less in\n  degC; the house-stocked RTD_PT100_3W_D6X50_3M probe is a Pt100 and\n  still works here - see the build options below.\n  A 2-wire probe (Pt1000, Pt100 or an NTC) is accommodated by fitting\n  R708 / R709, which tie the sense lead to the return at the connector.\n  Lead compensation is then lost; that is the lower-accuracy option."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 266.7 11.43 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5b838221-ab63-5278-b2af-c37f6024d95e")
	)
	(text
		"RATIOMETRIC 3-WIRE MEASUREMENT (ADS1120 SBAS535D section 9.2.2)\n  IDAC1 -> the AIN carrying the A lead, IDAC2 -> the AIN carrying the\n  B lead. Both currents return through the shared reference resistor\n  R707, so VREF = (IDAC1 + IDAC2) x R707 and the conversion result is\n  Code ~ R(RTD) x Gain / (2 x R707): independent of the IDAC value.\n  Because IDAC1 and IDAC2 are matched, the drop in lead A cancels the\n  drop in lead B and the lead resistance falls out.\n  This is the datasheet variant that routes the IDACs to the same\n  pins used for measurement, which is what lets ONE ADS1120 and ONE\n  reference resistor serve BOTH 3-wire RTDs (SBAS535D section 9.2.2:\n  \"even two 3-wire RTDs sharing the same reference resistor can be\n  measured with a single device\"). It requires the filter resistors\n  R701..R704 to be small and well matched, hence 100R 0.1%.\n\nDEFAULT BUILD - Pt1000        ALTERNATE BUILD - Pt100\n  IDAC1 = IDAC2 = 250 uA        IDAC1 = IDAC2 = 250 uA\n  R707 = 5k (fitted)            R707 = 5k (unchanged)\n  VREF = 2.5 V                  VREF = 2.5 V\n  Gain 4, FSR +/-625 mV         Gain 32, FSR +/-78.1 mV\n  1039..1155 ohm over 10..40 C  103.9..115.5 ohm over 10..40 C\n  260..289 mV at the PGA        26..29 mV at the PGA\nOnly the ADS1120 register settings differ - no BOM or layout change.\nGain 4 (not 8) is deliberate: it keeps the input inside FSR up to\n+200 degC, so a probe on warm structure cannot silently over-range.\nResolution is still 0.02 degC, 50x better than REQ-EL-07 needs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 266.7 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4ddb1e11-3d7b-56cc-8ba2-87b8ada51375")
	)
	(text
		"ERROR BUDGET AGAINST REQ-EL-07 (1 degC), Pt1000 build\n  Pt1000 class A at 40 degC            +/-0.23 degC\n  R707 tolerance 0.05%                 +/-0.14 degC\n  R707 drift, 5 ppm/degC over +/-15 C  +/-0.02 degC\n  R701..R704 mismatch, 0.2 ohm worst   +/-0.05 degC\n  ADS1120 INL 20 ppm FSR               +/-0.02 degC\n  RSS total                            +/-0.28 degC\n  Worst-case sum                       +/-0.46 degC\nADC gain error (0.1% max) and IDAC mismatch (0.3% max) are gain\nterms: they are removed either by a one-point calibration into the\nnvm_calibration EEPROM, or in firmware by IDAC rotation - swapping\nwhich IDAC drives which AIN between readings and averaging, which\nthis topology supports directly. Without either, IDAC mismatch\nalone would add up to +/-0.41 degC, still inside 1 degC.\nSelf-heating at 250 uA in 1000 ohm is 63 uW, under 0.02 degC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 266.7 118.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0efb2fd9-9cab-51fa-af86-d3aa9a7afb61")
	)
	(text
		"INTERFACE AND TEST NOTES\n  SPI2 is shared with motor_drive (DRV8323) - see ARCHITECTURE.md\n  section 5. R712..R715 (47R) are both the series terminators and\n  the SPI2 isolation links for this peripheral (TEST_PLAN 3.3).\n  ADS1120 DRDY has NO pin in the .ioc, so it is brought out to\n  TP707 only; firmware polls DOUT/DRDY instead. If an interrupt is\n  wanted later, allocate a spare GPIO in the .ioc and wire it here.\n  CLK is tied to DGND: the ADS1120 runs on its internal oscillator.\n  Firmware must leave the low-side power switch (PSW) off - it sits\n  between AIN3/REFN1 and AVSS, and AIN3 is a live input here.\n  TP701..TP704 probe leads, TP705/TP706 the ADC reference,\n  TP707..TP711 hooks on the SPI2 nets, TP712/TP713 GND hooks.\n  Substituting a fixed resistor for a probe (TEST_PLAN section 4) is\n  a push-in terminal operation - no soldering.\n  +5VA and +3V3 PWR_FLAGs live in loadcell_afe; both sheets consume\n  the same global rails from power_rails (OQ-02)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 266.7 158.75 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9f2011ae-d19f-5cf5-ae87-cefc915c8c42")
	)
